{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
By faith old Noah built an ark before the rain came down
[Gm]By faith went Ab[F]raham from home [Eb]across the unknown ground
By [Bb]faith the people crossed the sea as if on solid land
By [Gm]faith the walls of [F]Jericho fell [Eb]down at God's com[Bb]mand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Faith is the assurance of [Eb]what we hope [Bb]for
The [Gm]conviction of what we do not [F]see
[Bb]Small as a mustard [Eb]seed in my [Bb]hand
But it [Gm]rests on the One [F]who carries [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The apostles said to the Lord, Give us more faith
And he [Gm]spoke of the [F]smallest seed a far[Eb]mer ever [Bb]sows
If you have faith like a mustard seed
You will say to this mountain, [Gm]Move from here to there
[F]And it will [Eb]move
Nothing will be im[F]possible for [Bb]you
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [F] |
| [F] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Without [Gm]faith it is impossible to [Eb]please him
For [Bb]whoever comes to God must believe [F]that he exists
And that he re[Eb]wards those who seek [Bb]him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Faith is the assurance of [Eb]what we hope [Bb]for
The [Gm7]conviction of what we do not [F]see
[Bb]Small as a mustard [Eb]seed in my [Bb]hand
